From 6273b7f12eb1299c9b684f93d1ebc3ddcfa79863 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:44:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bend2: an asynchronous scheduler for waits that no file
 descriptor backs, and host-neutral I/O for page modules

A wait that no fd backs parks with at = Infinity (or a deadline) and is woken by io_notify, so an event loop can run it. The top-level run awaits; a nested run keeps the blocking poll.

A module that a page imports carries the runtime's input and output and the scheduler, and exports page_main, which runs main. The runtime looks up the host's modules (fs, tty, bun:ffi) when it uses them, through process.getBuiltinModule, and a page has none: its output goes to #bend-output (or console), and a system call throws.
